			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The &eScribe's Table&r is where spells actually get written - drag glyphs onto a page, arrange the order, and bind the finished spell to your book."
				""
				"&e&lSpells are built from three kinds of glyph, in this order:&r"
				"&71. &fForm&7 - how the spell is delivered. &lEvery spell must start with one.&r Projectile, Touch, Self, Burst."
				"&72. &fEffect&7 - what it actually does. Break, Harm, Grow, Ignite, Place Block."
				"&73. &fAugment&7 - modifies the effect before it. Amplify, Extend Time, AOE, Pierce, Dampen."
				""
				"&e&lThe order matters enormously.&r Augments apply to the effect immediately before them, so &7Projectile - Break - AOE&r breaks a wide area where it lands, while &7Projectile - AOE - Break&r does something quite different."
				""
				"&e&lMana cost rises steeply with augments&r, so a spell that reads well on paper may be uncastable. Check the cost shown on the table before you commit."
				""
				"&7This is the mod's whole appeal: you are not picking spells off a list, you are designing them. A &fProjectile - Break - Fortune&7 wand is a mining tool nobody handed you.&r"
				""
				"&8Start simple. Two-glyph spells are cheap, cast fast, and cover most practical needs."
			]
			icon: "ars_nouveau:scribes_table"
			id: "00C017B9AE1AFE32"
			rewards: [{
				id: "06BF369D06FF9A71"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Where spells get written"
			tasks: [{
				id: "15DDE434F5B859E9"
				item: "ars_nouveau:scribes_table"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&dThe Scribe's Table"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"An &eArcane Pedestal&r channels source into ritual crafting - the entry point to Ars Nouveau's item-enchanting and automation side."
				""
				"&e&lThe standard layout:&r an &7Enchanting Apparatus&r in the centre with &7Arcane Pedestals&r ringing it. Put the reagent in the apparatus, one ingredient on each pedestal, and provide Source. Right-click the apparatus to run it."
				""
				"&e&lSource is Ars Nouveau's power&r and it is entirely separate from FE. You generate it with &7Source Jars&r fed by things like the Volcanic Sourcelink (burns items) or Agronomic Sourcelink (nearby crop growth). Rituals will silently fail with no source nearby."
				""
				"&e&lWhat this unlocks:&r spell parchment, upgraded wands and armour, Ritual Braziers, and the automation side - &7Whirlisprigs&r that farm for you and &7Drygmys&r that collect mob drops without killing anything."
				""
				"&7The Drygmy is the standout for a void world: it gathers drops from nearby mobs passively, which is a mob farm with no grinder, no fall damage and no spawn platform.&r"
				""
				"&8Craft the Worn Notebook early - it is the in-game documentation and covers every glyph and ritual in far more detail than a quest book reasonably can."
			]
			icon: "ars_nouveau:arcane_pedestal"
			id: "17478CA1F714EBAB"
			rewards: [{
				id: "795B8C8AA7F9DD36"
				type: "xp_levels"
				xp_levels: 3
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "&7Ritual crafting"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0DFBFFBD8702CC7C"
				item: "ars_nouveau:arcane_pedestal"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&dArcane Pedestal"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1BD3F090A3FA8B3C"]
			description: [
				"&eBotania&r is magic that behaves like a tech mod, which makes it the natural companion to Ars Nouveau rather than a rival."
				""
				"Everything runs on &eMana&r, generated by flowers and moved around by &eSpreaders&r firing visible bursts across your island. Start with &eLivingrock&r, a &eMana Pool&r to hold it and a &eSpreader&r to move it."
				""
				"&7Botania has no power cables, no GUIs and no config screens. Every machine is a flower, and everything it does happens in the world where you can watch it."
			]
			icon: "botania:mana_pool"
			id: "7E30500000000001"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E30500000000101"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "&7Magic that acts like machinery"
			tasks: [
